\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Not-to-scale timing schematic of the asynchronous perception--control architecture. Frames and inference results were exchanged through bounded queues, while the nominal 200-Hz supervisory loop polled the result queue without blocking. The first threshold-qualified result ($\geq 0.25$ confidence) triggered a single strategy-level update, after which the selected strategy remained locked for the trial; impedance parameters transitioned over approximately 300 ms. The schematic shows nominal module timing; end-to-end trigger latency was not measured.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:2}{{2}{4}{}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsubsection}{\numberline {2.2.4}Gripper-execution channel}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
